<!-- HERO -->
<div class="page-hero">
  <p>Diamond Education</p>
  <h1>The 4 Cs of <em>Diamonds</em></h1>
  <p class="hero-sub">Everything you need to know to choose a diamond that reflects your unique style, personality, and budget.</p>
</div>

<!-- INTRO -->
<div class="intro-strip">
  <p>At Melia Nae Jewellers, we believe in helping you choose the perfect diamond. The 4 Cs — Cut, Clarity, Colour, and Carat — are the key factors that determine a diamond's beauty, brilliance, and value.</p>
</div>

<!-- 4 Cs NAV -->
<div class="cs-nav">
  <div class="cs-nav-item active" data-target="section-cut"><span class="cs-num">C</span><span class="cs-label">Cut</span></div>
  <div class="cs-nav-item" data-target="section-clarity"><span class="cs-num">C</span><span class="cs-label">Clarity</span></div>
  <div class="cs-nav-item" data-target="section-color"><span class="cs-num">C</span><span class="cs-label">Colour</span></div>
  <div class="cs-nav-item" data-target="section-carat"><span class="cs-num">C</span><span class="cs-label">Carat</span></div>
</div>

<!-- 1. CUT -->
<div class="cs-section" id="section-cut">
  <div class="cs-content">
    <div class="cs-number">01</div>
    <p class="cs-eyebrow">The Sparkle Factor</p>
    <h2><em>Cut</em></h2>
    <p class="cs-tagline">The most important of the 4 Cs</p>
    <p>The cut of a diamond is the most crucial aspect when it comes to its sparkle. It refers to how well a diamond's facets are shaped and aligned. A well-cut diamond reflects light beautifully, creating stunning brilliance.</p>
    <div class="cs-grades">
      <h4>Cut Grades</h4>
      <div class="grade-row"><span class="grade-badge gold">Ideal</span><span>Exceptional sparkle and symmetry</span></div>
      <div class="grade-row"><span class="grade-badge">Very Good</span><span>Beautiful sparkle with excellent symmetry</span></div>
      <div class="grade-row"><span class="grade-badge mid">Good</span><span>Adequate brilliance with solid symmetry</span></div>
      <div class="grade-row"><span class="grade-badge light">Poor</span><span>Minimal sparkle due to poor symmetry</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pro-tip">
      <strong>✦ Pro Tip</strong>
      <p>Prioritise cut over carat size. A smaller diamond with an excellent cut will shine brighter than a larger one with a poor cut.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cs-visual">
    <div class="sparkle-grid">
      <div class="sparkle-cell"><div class="spark">✦</div><div class="spark-label">Ideal</div></div>
      <div class="sparkle-cell"><div class="spark">✧</div><div class="spark-label">Very Good</div></div>
      <div class="sparkle-cell"><div class="spark">◆</div><div class="spark-label">Good</div></div>
      <div class="sparkle-cell"><div class="spark">◇</div><div class="spark-label">Poor</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- 2. CLARITY -->
<div class="cs-section" id="section-clarity">
  <div class="cs-content">
    <div class="cs-number">02</div>
    <p class="cs-eyebrow">Flawlessness You Can See</p>
    <h2><em>Clarity</em></h2>
    <p class="cs-tagline">The fewer inclusions, the more it shines</p>
    <p>Clarity measures the presence of internal imperfections, or inclusions. While tiny inclusions are common, diamonds with fewer or no visible inclusions are more valuable. The clearer the diamond, the more it will shine.</p>
    <div class="cs-grades">
      <h4>Clarity Grades</h4>
      <div class="grade-row"><span class="grade-badge gold">FL</span><span>Flawless — no visible imperfections</span></div>
      <div class="grade-row"><span class="grade-badge">VVS1/VVS2</span><span>Inclusions difficult to see under magnification</span></div>
      <div class="grade-row"><span class="grade-badge mid">VS1/VS2</span><span>Small inclusions, still eye-clean</span></div>
      <div class="grade-row"><span class="grade-badge light">SI1/SI2</span><span>Inclusions visible to the naked eye</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pro-tip">
      <strong>✦ Pro Tip</strong>
      <p>For the best value, choose diamonds with clarity grades of VS1 or higher — they look flawless to the naked eye without the FL price tag.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cs-visual">
    <div class="cs-visual-block">
      <div class="diamond-icon">◈</div>
      <div class="diamond-label">Eye-clean from VS1</div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- 3. COLOR -->
<div class="cs-section" id="section-color">
  <div class="cs-content">
    <div class="cs-number">03</div>
    <p class="cs-eyebrow">Pure or Warm</p>
    <h2><em>Colour</em></h2>
    <p class="cs-tagline">D (colourless) to Z (light yellow)</p>
    <p>Diamonds are graded on a scale from D (colourless) to Z (light yellow or brown). The more colourless a diamond, the higher its value. However, slight warmth can be less noticeable in certain settings.</p>
    <div class="cs-grades">
      <h4>Color Grades</h4>
      <div class="grade-row"><span class="grade-badge gold">D–F</span><span>Colorless — ideal for white gold or platinum</span></div>
      <div class="grade-row"><span class="grade-badge">G–J</span><span>Near-colourless — great for yellow or rose gold</span></div>
      <div class="grade-row"><span class="grade-badge light">K–Z</span><span>Noticeable warmth — pairs well with yellow gold</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pro-tip">
      <strong>✦ Pro Tip</strong>
      <p>For the purest white diamond, go for D–F grades, especially when set in white metal like platinum or white gold.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cs-visual">
    <div class="color-bar">
      <div class="color-row"><div class="color-swatch" style="background: rgba(255,255,255,0.95); border: 1px solid var(--border);"></div><span>D–F &nbsp;Colorless</span></div>
      <div class="color-row"><div class="color-swatch" style="background: rgba(255,252,245,0.95); border: 1px solid var(--border);"></div><span>G–J &nbsp;Near-colourless</span></div>
      <div class="color-row"><div class="color-swatch" style="background: rgba(255,245,210,0.9); border: 1px solid var(--border);"></div><span>K–M &nbsp;Faint yellow</span></div>
      <div class="color-row"><div class="color-swatch" style="background: rgba(255,235,160,0.85); border: 1px solid var(--border);"></div><span>N–Z &nbsp;Light yellow</span></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- 4. CARAT -->
<div class="cs-section" id="section-carat">
  <div class="cs-content">
    <div class="cs-number">04</div>
    <p class="cs-eyebrow">Size &amp; Weight</p>
    <h2><em>Carat</em></h2>
    <p class="cs-tagline">Bigger isn't always better</p>
    <p>Carat measures the weight of a diamond, not its size. Larger diamonds are rarer and more expensive, but the right cut can make a smaller diamond appear larger. Remember — cut, clarity, and color matter just as much.</p>
    <div class="cs-grades">
      <h4>Carat Guide</h4>
      <div class="grade-row"><span class="grade-badge gold">0.25–0.50</span><span>Ideal for first-time buyers; excellent sparkle</span></div>
      <div class="grade-row"><span class="grade-badge">1 CT</span><span>Classic size for engagement rings</span></div>
      <div class="grade-row"><span class="grade-badge mid">2–5 CT</span><span>Clarity and cut should be top priority</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="pro-tip">
      <strong>✦ Pro Tip</strong>
      <p>A diamond just shy of your target carat (like 0.95 CT instead of 1 CT) can offer significant savings with little visible difference.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
